   \begin{enumerate}
       \item The state evolution parameters converge $q_t \to q_{\ast}\in\RR^L$, where $q_{\ast}$ is the solution to the following fixed-point equation
       \begin{equation}
           q_{\ast} = 1 - \diag\sbr{\rbr{\Diag\rbr{\lambda\odot q_{\ast}}+B^{-1}}^{-1}}.
       \end{equation}
       In comparison with our self-consistent equations \eqref{eq: self-consistent eq matrix}, it holds that $q_{\ast}^{(l)}=1-M_{ll}(1)$.

